{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"Recall that the formula for arc length of $\\displaystyle~f(t)~$ over $\\displaystyle~[a, b]~$ is\n\n$\\displaystyle L=\\int_a^b\\sqrt{1+\\big[f\\,^\\prime(t)\\big]^2}~dx\\,$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"First calculate $\\displaystyle~f\\,^\\prime(t)$ and simplify.\n\n$\\displaystyle f\\,^\\prime(t)=\\dfrac{t^2(-2)-(1-2t)\\cdot2t}{(t^2)^2}=\\dfrac{2t^2-2t}{t^4}=\\dfrac{2t-2}{t^3}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Next, use the formula above to write the integral expression that gives the arc length in question.\n\n$L=\\displaystyle\\int_{a}^b\\sqrt{1+\\bigg(\\dfrac{2t-2}{t^3}\\bigg)^2}~dt$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Which integral gives the length of the graph of $f(t)=\\dfrac{1-2t}{t^2}$ between $t=a$ and $t=b$?**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$\\displaystyle \\int_a^b\\sqrt{1+\\bigg(\\dfrac{-2-2t}{t^3}\\bigg)^2}~dt$","correct":false},{"content":"$\\displaystyle \\int_a^b\\sqrt{1+\\dfrac{2-2t}{t^3}}~dt$","correct":false},{"content":"$\\displaystyle \\int_a^b\\sqrt{1+\\bigg(\\dfrac{2t-2}{t^3}\\bigg)^2}~dt$","correct":true},{"content":"$\\displaystyle \\int_a^b\\sqrt{1+\\dfrac{2t-2}{t^3}~}~dt$","correct":false}],"countChoices":false,"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
